I've fixed both problems: a failed reaction save now rolls the UI back and shows an error, and one click no longer saves twice. The existing test suites for record detail, i18n and plugin-detail pass (3552 tests). No new test exercises the failure, rapid-click or StrictMode paths, and I haven't clicked through it in the running app.

**What was wrong** (`packages/app-shell/src/views/RecordDetailView.tsx`, `handleToggleReaction`):
- **Saving twice:** the save to the server was started from inside a React state update function. React can run that function twice (it always does in development's StrictMode), so one click could send two saves.
- **No error:** the save's failure was caught and ignored, so the optimistic reaction stayed on screen even though nothing was stored.

**What changed:**
- **Queued clicks:** each comment now has its own queue of clicks, and each click records which emoji was toggled. The UI updates right away, and clicks made while a save is in progress are queued, not dropped or disabled.
- **One save at a time:** saves run in order, one per click, outside any state update. Each applies its toggle to the last state the server actually confirmed, so a later save is never built on a failed one.
- **What you see:** the comment shows the stored reactions with any clicks still being saved applied on top.
- **On failure:** that click is dropped, an error toast says "Your reaction was not saved. Please try again.", and the comment is redrawn from the stored state.
- **Translations:** I added a `detail.reactionFailed` message to all 10 locale files.

Because the server confirms each click in turn, toggling an emoji on and off quickly sends two saves rather than combining them into one. Every click is still stored.

Running `tsc` on app-shell reports many errors, because the other workspace packages it imports haven't been built. None of them are in the code I changed. Nothing is committed.
